INT. NORTHSIDE REC CENTER - GYM - DAY

Squeaking sneakers. A basketball THUMPS. Nobody's playing.

Jaylen, 17, sits on the bottom bleacher, thumbs flying. Group chat blowing up. Forty-one unread.

Her phone. Buzzing. Buzzing. Buzzing.

Priya, 17, tall, hoodie up, drops next to him.

PRIYA
So are you gonna answer or just let it ghost you?

JAYLEN
It's the whole team. They all saw the screenshot.

PRIYA
Delete the app.

JAYLEN
Priya, my lawyer said don't delete anything. Literal evidence.

PRIYA
Your lawyer's like twenty-six and she says "no cap."

JAYLEN
She's good, though.

Silence. The ball rolls across the floor and stops.

Nothing.

Jaylen locks the phone. Face down on his knee.

This is the part where it stops being funny.

Priya nudges him.

PRIYA (CONT'D)
For real, tho. You didn't do it.

JAYLEN
Everyone thinks I did.

The double doors BANG open. MS. ADEYEMI, 40s, blazer, folder under her arm, strides in. The lawyer.

MS. ADEYEMI
Jaylen. Deposition's moved to Thursday. Good news.

JAYLEN
(small)
Okay.

MS. ADEYEMI
Put the phone away, Priya.

PRIYA
I'm literally not on it.

Ms. Adeyemi sits on the bleacher above them. Pulls out a pen.

MS. ADEYEMI
Start from the beginning.
